### Relations
Relations define how entities relate to each other. They are also defined using functions from `@interaqt/shared`.

```typescript
import { Relation } from '@interaqt/shared';

const UserPosts = Relation({
  name: 'UserPosts',
  properties: {
    source: User,
    target: Post,
    type: '1:n' // One-to-many
  }
});
```

### Computations
Computations are reactive derived data. They automatically update when their dependencies change. Computations can be defined at the entity level or the global level.

```typescript
import { Computation } from '@interaqt/shared';

const UserPostCount = Computation({
  name: 'UserPostCount',
  description: 'Total number of posts for each user',
  relation: UserPosts,
  attribute: 'count',
});
